# One line ending everywhere.
#
# The project now moves between the Windows ComfyUI install and a Mac. Without
# this, every text file rewrites itself on each checkout and every diff is a
# whole-file diff — noise that hides the changes that matter. The index is
# already pure LF (verified: 0 files stored with CRLF), so this freezes the
# state the repository is in rather than converting anything.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Except the decision tables. `csv.writer`'s own line ending is CRLF and
# `shotlist.write_csv` keeps it, so storing these as LF would make every save
# from the Storyline panel a whole-file diff — which is exactly the noise the
# rule above exists to remove. Matters from 2026-09-03, when
# projects/first_reel became the first project whose shots.csv is in git.
*.csv  text eol=crlf

# Never line-ending-converted, never diffed as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ttf  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.mp4  binary
